    "explanation": "Common indications for an emergent cesarean section\ninclude:\n• Abruption\n• Fetal bradycardia\n• Umbilical cord prolapse\n• Uterine rupture\n• Hemorrhage from a placenta previa\nPreeclampsia with severe features does not necessitate\ncesarean delivery; induction of labor is recommended if\ndelivery is needed.",
