    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "Acute pyelonephritis is defined as infection of the renal\nparenchyma and pelvicalyceal system.\nIt is typically accompanied by fever and flank or back pain,\nin addition to symptoms of lower urinary tract infection.\nRecommended regimens are as follows:\n• Ciprofloxacin 500 mg twice daily for 7 days\n• Ciprofloxacin 1000 mg daily for 7 days\n• Levofloxacin 750 mg daily for 5 days\n• Trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole DS 160/800 mg twice\ndaily for 14 days\nThe other choices are recommended treatment regimens\nfor uncomplicated cystitis.",
