    "subject": "obstetrics-gynecology",
    "originalNumber": 41,
    "stem": "Which of the following HPV types is\nmore associated with squamous cell\ncarcinoma of the cervix?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "HPV 6"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "HPV 11"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "HPV 16"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "HPV 18"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "HPV is the primary etiologic infectious agent associated with\ncervical cancer.\nThe low-risk HPV types are HPV 6 and HPV 11 whereas HPV\n16 and 18 are more commonly associated with a higher risk\nfor cervical cancer.\nHPV 16 is more commonly associated with squamous cell\ncarcinoma of the cervix.\nOn the other hand, HPV 18 is a risk factor for cervical\nadenocarcinoma.\nCervical cancer is the most common gynecologic cancer in\nwomen worldwide.",
