    "explanation": "One quantifiable method to predict labor induction outcomes\nis the score described by Bishop.\nAs favorability—or Bishop score—rises, the rate of induction\nto effect vaginal delivery also increases.\nA Bishop score >8 conveys a high likelihood for a successful\ninduction, and a score ≤6 is considered unfavorable.",
