    "explanation": "Puberty is considered delayed if no secondary sexual characteristics are noted by age 13, which is more than two standard deviations from the mean age, or if menses have not commenced by age 16.\nDelayed puberty affects 3 percent of adolescents. Causes include chronic anovulation, constitutional delay, anatomic abnormalities, hypergonadotropic hypogonadism, and hypogonadotropic hypogonadism.",
