    "subject": "obstetrics-gynecology",
    "originalNumber": 22,
    "stem": "The biophysical scoring (BPS) uses the following parameters:",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "I, III"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "II, III"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "I, II"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "I, II, III"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "D",
    "explanation": "This is the correct choice. It includes all three parameters of the Biophysical Profile: fetal movement (I), fetal breathing (II), and amniotic fluid index (III). Each component contributes to the overall assessment of fetal well-being.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "This combination includes fetal movement (I) and amniotic fluid index (III). It is not complete, as it omits fetal breathing (II), which is also a component of the Biophysical Profile.",
      "B": "This combination includes fetal breathing (II) and amniotic fluid index (III). While both are components, it omits fetal movement (I), which is an essential parameter in the Biophysical Profile.",
      "C": "This combination includes fetal movement (I) and fetal breathing (II). It is also incomplete, as it omits the assessment of the amniotic fluid index (III).",
      "D": "This is the correct choice. It includes all three parameters of the Biophysical Profile: fetal movement (I), fetal breathing (II), and amniotic fluid index (III). Each component contributes to the overall assessment of fetal well-being."
    },
