    "id": "notion-obstetrics-gynecology-0027",
    "subject": "obstetrics-gynecology",
    "originalNumber": 27,
    "stem": "Mara has been diagnosed with unruptured tubal ectopic pregnancy. Laparotomy was performed where the affected fallopian tube was incised and the ectopic gestation is removed. The procedure is called .",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Oophorocystectomy"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Salpingectomy"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Salpingostomy"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Medical management"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Salpingostomy involves making an incision into the fallopian tube to remove an ectopic pregnancy while preserving the tube. It is a procedure where the surgeon opens the tube, removes the ectopic pregnancy, and then closes the tube. In this case, since the question mentions that the affected fallopian tube was incised and the ectopic gestation was removed, salpingostomy is the correct term. The removal of the tube is described as salpingectomy.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "Oophorocystectomy involves the removal of an ovarian cyst. It is not the correct term for the surgical procedure performed in the case of an unruptured tubal ectopic pregnancy.",
      "B": "Salpingectomy is the surgical removal of the fallopian tube. In the context of an unruptured tubal ectopic pregnancy, if the fallopian tube is affected, removing the tube is a common approach to address the ectopic gestation and prevent future ectopic pregnancies in that tube.",
      "C": "Salpingostomy involves making an incision into the fallopian tube to remove an ectopic pregnancy while preserving the tube. It is a procedure where the surgeon opens the tube, removes the ectopic pregnancy, and then closes the tube. In this case, since the question mentions that the affected fallopian tube was incised and the ectopic gestation was removed, salpingostomy is the correct term. The removal of the tube is described as salpingectomy.",
      "D": "Medical management refers to the use of medications, such as methotrexate, to treat an ectopic pregnancy. It is a non-surgical option and may be considered in certain cases, especially if the ectopic pregnancy is detected early, is unruptured, and the patient is stable. However, in the scenario described in the question, laparotomy was performed, indicating a surgical approach."
    },
