    "id": "notion-obstetrics-gynecology-0067",
    "subject": "obstetrics-gynecology",
    "originalNumber": 67,
    "stem": "A wet mount of the vaginal discharge treated with KOH. Microscopic examination of the slide shows hyphae. The most probable diagnosis is",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Giardiasis"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Bacterial vaginosis"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Vaginal candidiasis"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Trichomoniasis"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Vaginal candidiasis, commonly known as a yeast infection, is caused by the overgrowth of Candida species, most commonly Candida albicans. The characteristic hyphae and spores of Candida can be visualized in a wet mount treated with KOH. This finding supports the diagnosis of vaginal candidiasis.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "Giardiasis is caused by the protozoan parasite Giardia lamblia. It primarily affects the small intestine and is associated with diarrhea. However, Giardia lamblia is not a fungus, and its presence would not be identified in a KOH-treated wet mount.",
      "B": "Bacterial vaginosis is a common condition characterized by an overgrowth of certain bacteria in the vagina. It typically presents with a malodorous discharge. Bacterial vaginosis is caused by bacteria, not fungi, so hyphae would not be observed in a wet mount.",
      "C": "Vaginal candidiasis, commonly known as a yeast infection, is caused by the overgrowth of Candida species, most commonly Candida albicans. The characteristic hyphae and spores of Candida can be visualized in a wet mount treated with KOH. This finding supports the diagnosis of vaginal candidiasis.",
      "D": "Trichomoniasis is a sexually transmitted infection caused by the protozoan parasite Trichomonas vaginalis. It is associated with a frothy, malodorous discharge. However, Trichomonas vaginalis is not a fungus, and hyphae would not be observed in a wet mount."
    },
