    "id": "notion-obstetrics-gynecology-0091",
    "subject": "obstetrics-gynecology",
    "originalNumber": 91,
    "stem": "Which of the following lowers the serum calcium level in the body by facilitating bone remodeling?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Vitamin B"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Calcitonin"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Vitamin D"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Parathyroid hormone"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "B",
    "explanation": "Calcitonin is a hormone produced by the thyroid gland.\nIt functions to lower blood calcium levels by inhibiting the activity of osteoclasts (cells that break down bone) and promoting calcium deposition in bones.\nOverall, calcitonin helps regulate calcium homeostasis by favoring bone formation.",
    "choiceRationales": {
      "A": "Vitamin B is a group of water-soluble vitamins, and it doesn't play a direct role in calcium metabolism or bone remodeling.\nIt is involved in various metabolic processes in the body, but it does not influence serum calcium levels.",
      "B": "Calcitonin is a hormone produced by the thyroid gland.\nIt functions to lower blood calcium levels by inhibiting the activity of osteoclasts (cells that break down bone) and promoting calcium deposition in bones.\nOverall, calcitonin helps regulate calcium homeostasis by favoring bone formation.",
      "C": "Vitamin D is essential for the absorption of calcium from the intestines and its deposition in bones.\nWhile it promotes calcium absorption, it tends to increase serum calcium levels rather than lower them.",
      "D": "PTH is produced by the parathyroid glands and has the opposite effect of calcitonin.\nPTH increases blood calcium levels by promoting the release of calcium from bones, increasing calcium absorption from the intestines, and reducing calcium loss in urine."
    },
