    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "This case describes fetal hydantoin syndrome. It is\ndue to ingestion of the antiseizure drug phenytoin.\nEthanol – Fetal alcohol syndrome\nLithium – Ebstein anomaly\nPhenytoin – Fetal hydantoin syndrome\nThalidomide – phocomelia\nMethimazole – aplasia cutis congenita\nSource: Topnotch handout on pharmacology",
