    "subject": "obstetrics-gynecology",
    "originalNumber": 5,
    "stem": "A 25 yr old female presents with vaginal spotting\nand RLQ pain. A TVS is done which shows empty\nuterus. Serum HCG was 4000mIU/ml. Which of the\nfollowing is not a risk factor for her condition?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "PID"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Previous similar diagnosis"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "IUD use"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Congenital malformation of the uterus"
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "None of the above"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "E",
    "explanation": "This is a case of ectopic pregnancy. The absence of a\ngestational sac inside the uterus with TVS when the\nHCG level is >1500mIU/mL is 100% accurate in\nexcluding a lie uterine pregnancy. An investigation\nmust be carried out to rule out ectopic pregnancy.\nSource: Williams Obstetrics 23RD ed p 244",
