    "explanation": "Kallman's syndrome is the congenital absence of\nGnRH producing cells causing primary amenorrhea\nassociated with anosmia. Sheehan's syndrome is\nhypopituitarism caused by ischemic necrosis of the\npituitary gland. Ashermann's syndrome is\nintrauterine adhesions usually from repeated\ncurettage.",
