    "subject": "obstetrics-gynecology",
    "originalNumber": 205,
    "stem": "A 27 year-old G3P2(2002) at 34 weeks and 5 days\nage of gestation presents to the emergency\ndepartment due to labor pains. IE findings are: 4\ncm dilated, 70% effaced, cephalic, station -2,\nruptured bag of water. What is the best course of\naction?",
