    "subject": "obstetrics-gynecology",
    "originalNumber": 208,
    "stem": "A 25 year old G1P0 at 37 weeks and 6 days of AOG\npresents to the emergency department due to\nlabor pains. BP was 200/120. Dipstick analysis of\nurine revelaed 3+ proteinuria. Patient complains of\nblurred vision and severe epigastric pain. How\nshould magnesium sulfate be given for this\npatient?",
