    "subject": "obstetrics-gynecology",
    "originalNumber": 211,
    "stem": "A 28 year-old G3P2 (2002) at 38 weeks and 4 days\nAOG came in due to vaginal bleeding. Her first\npregnancy was delivered via low-transverse\ncesarean section due to malpresentation. For the\nsecond pregnancy, she delivered vaginally a\nhealthy baby girl. At present, IE findings are: 5 cm\ndilated, 80% effaced, cephalic, station -2, intact bag\nof water. Which factor makes this patient a\ncandidate for normal spontaenous delivery?",
