    "stem": "A 37 year old G3P1 (1011), 39 weeks AOG, was\nadmitted due to labor pains. VS are normal. FH 35\ncm, FHT 145 bpm. IE: Cervix 3-4 cm dilated 70%\neffaced, ROT, st -2, (+) BOW. Labor admission test\nshowed reassuring fetal heart rate pattern. 2 hours\nafter a repeat IE was done: cervix 5 cm dilated 80%\neffaced, ROT, st -1, (+) BOW, FHT 140 bpm. After\nanother 2 hours, a repeat IE was done: cervix 6 cm\ndilated, 90% effaced, ROA, st-1, (+) BOW, FHT 143\nbpm. EFM tracing showed a reassuring fetal heart\nrate pattern with 190 Montevideo Units. How\nwould you diagnose the labor pattern of the\npatient?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Normal labor pattern"
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "Arrest in cervical dilatation"
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Protracted cervical dilatation"
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "Prolonged latent phase"
      },
      {
        "label": "E",
        "text": "Arrest in descent"
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "Once in the active phase: rate of cervical dilatation\nshould be 1.5 cm/hour for multiparas.",
