    "correctChoice": "A",
    "explanation": "Ectopic pregnancy is the implanation of trophoblast\nother than the endometrium of the uterine cavity.\nThe most frequent site is ampulla of the fallopian\ntube. Clinical manifestations begin at 6-8 weeks\nwith the triad of amenorrhea, vaginal bleeding and\nabdominal pain.",
