    "id": "superexam-obstetrics-gynecology-0547",
    "subject": "obstetrics-gynecology",
    "originalNumber": 547,
    "stem": "Which of the following INCORRECTLY describes\nthe perineum?",
    "choices": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "The pelvic diaphragm consists of the levator ani\nmuscles plus the coccygeus muscles posteriorly."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "The levator ani muscles form a broad muscular\nsling that originates from the posteriorsurface of\nthe superior pubic rami, from the inner surface of\nthe ischial spine, and between these two sites, from\nthe obturator fascia."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "The major blood supply to the perineum is via\nthe internal pudendal artery and its branches.\nThese include the posterior rectal artery and\ninferior labial artery."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "The innervation of the perineum is primarily via\nthe pudendal nerve and its branches. The pudendal\nnerve originates from the S2, S3, and S4 level of the\nspinal cord."
      }
    ],
    "correctChoice": "C",
    "explanation": "there is no posterior rectal and inferior labial\narteries. Its supposed to be inferior rectal and\nposterior labial",
